# Mechatron Prime CI — real x86_64-linux flake checks verified by
# `nix flake show`; package build, Zig tests, and Windows cross-link coverage.
#
# The Zig unit tests are gated in BOTH optimize modes on purpose. libjxlz ships
# ReleaseSafe binaries, but Zig consumers (jpegz) compile this code at whatever
# mode they pass down, and `undefined` memory behaves differently per mode: a
# ReleaseFast-only encoder failure hid behind a ReleaseSafe-only gate until
# 2026-08-01. A future ReleaseFast release also needs that mode verified
# continuously rather than re-hunted at release time.
